 there are friends who  are suffering  it should remind us how deadly this  virus can be and and is and it should  remind us that we definitely have to  take measures to really prevent future  deaths from this disease  and if we  put this number into a international  context where does germany find itself  there  i think it's very difficult to compare  countries as to cultural differences  differences in availability of vaccines  vaccine rates etc it's definitely too  high and we really need to understand  how  serious this disease is  now obviously a medical crisis of these  proportions will cause suffering and  will have victims nevertheless how many  of these 100 000 deaths  would have been avoidable  it's a good question it's very difficult  to precisely estimate many many of those  certainly could have been avoided  specifically after we had vaccinations  and now the the real issue is that we  should  um understand that we can avoid future  deaths if we pick up the vaccination  rate if we take some measures to really  get the numbers down because many more  unfortunately will die in the future  germany does have a vaccination rate  below 70  uh below the eu average that certainly  seems to play a role here now let's look  at the current situation much is not yet  clear when it comes to the newly  discovered omicron variant how do you  expect it to impact the course of the  pandemic in this country  it's very difficult to estimate at this  point as we do not have all the numbers  that we need to make proper estimation  certainly it's of concern in particular  if you have a situation right now where  you have high number of new cases every  day where the hospitals are full and the  society is really um on its edge so we  need to make sure that the numbers are  going down now should omicron really  have the impact that we all fear  when the delta variant first was  discovered there were experts saying  well it might be more infectious  but less lethal is that something that  could apply to the omicron variant as  well  i think this is speculation right now we  know for sure omicron is here in germany  already probably has been here for  several weeks and there's a certain  concern that this variant will take over  as delta took over a few months ago  whether this is more severe or more  deadly is something that we need to  carefully evaluate  when the world health organization warns  that omicron may have a high likelihood  of immune escape from antibody mediated  protection what does that mean  it means that the vaccines may not be as  effective as against the delta variant  or the vile variant that we had in in  the beginning so we definitely need to  make sure that we understand that these  may come up do we need to get vaccinated  we need to get the booster shots it's  really important now to watch the  situation and to collect data to uh then  make proper uh consequences for on the  population level  tobias as people are arriving on flights  from south africa and neighboring  countries and they're sent to quarantine  because of the omicron variant what  progress have we made when it comes to  containing the virus through such  surveillance  i think first of all it's important that  this is not a south african problem  south africa was able to detect this  variant and shows the  really good surveillance system that  they have omicron certainly is in other  regions of the world already  but also it shows that the international  community  has learned and has taken action quickly  to really react to this whether the  action is enough or or proper is  something that we have to evaluate daily  to not making these regions in the world  or specifically south africa suffering  more than necessary  now if we look at the situation here in  germany there are some experts saying  that another hundred thousand people  will die of covet 19 in germany before  this whole pandemic will be over you  yourself are skeptical as well how  reliable is such a figure and what does  it depend on  not to happen for that matter  well those figures come from  mathematical models that project into  the future those models depend strongly  on assumptions so if we all get  vaccinated if we all get a booster shot  and in the future there will be modified  vaccinations available this number  hopefully will not be reality however  there are certain scenarios where this  number may in fact be reality so we  definitely have to be on alert and  evaluate the situation very carefully  today and in the future  tobias court director of the institute  of public health at berlin's charity  hospital thank you for talking to us  thank you for having me  dying of covet 19 has been the sad fate  of millions of people around the world  but many  more have fallen ill and survived and  that is one issue that one of your  questions for our science correspondent  derek williams touches on  [Music]  what's the survival rate of kovit 19 how  is it calculated  scientists who work with data on  mortality rates related to covet 19 they  generally don't use the term  survival rate although it is a common  one in evaluating other diseases like  cancer for example  according to cancer.net  the five-year survival rate for  pancreatic cancer  is 10 percent that's the percentage of  people who are diagnosed with it who are  still living at the end of those five  years  but epidemiologists dealing with a  pandemic disease where large numbers of  people also recover  they generally talk instead about other  numbers especially what's called  the case fatality rate or the cfr now  it's calculated  by dividing the number of confirmed  deaths from the disease  by the number of people diagnosed with  it by a test so clear background numbers  as this graphic from our world and data  shows cfrs have generally fallen in most  countries over time  from the early days of the pandemic that  mostly reflects the fact that doctors  have gotten a lot better at treating the  disease since it first appeared  in germany this credible source says  that at the moment  the cfr is around 1.8 percent now  that doesn't sound like much but think  about it for a second if correct  it means covid19 is currently killing  about 18  out of every thousand people diagnosed  with it here which makes it about 10  times more lethal than seasonal flu  and when you have tens of thousands of  people being newly diagnosed every day  like at the moment in germany  the numbers of those dying from it will  start to add up  very fast  very soon of course  most people who get the disease will  survive it but that's also highly  dependent the experts say  on factors like your own personal age  and your health and whether you've been  vaccinated so  talking about general survival rates and  trying to apply the concept to predict  your own chances of survival if you're  infected  doesn't really make sense  [Music]
 

